  "description": "HiQPdf Library for .NET (Classic) is a fast and flexible tool for creating high-quality PDF documents and converting HTML to PDF in .NET Framework, .NET Core and .NET Standard applications on Windows.\n\nThe library uses the Classic rendering engine to convert HTML to PDF, images and SVG.\n\nThe same HiQPdf API runs on the Chromium-based engine of HiQPdf Next, on Windows, Linux and macOS, in the HiQPdf.Windows, HiQPdf.Windows.Arm64, HiQPdf.Linux, HiQPdf.Linux.Arm64 and HiQPdf.MacOS packages: an application keeps its code and changes only the package reference.\n\nFor Windows, Linux and macOS, on x64 and ARM64, HiQPdf Next offers a newer Chromium-based rendering engine for modern HTML, CSS and JavaScript in the multi-platform package HiQPdf.Next.HtmlToPdf and in the platform packages HiQPdf.Next.HtmlToPdf.Windows, HiQPdf.Next.HtmlToPdf.Windows.Arm64, HiQPdf.Next.HtmlToPdf.Linux, HiQPdf.Next.HtmlToPdf.Linux.Arm64 and HiQPdf.Next.HtmlToPdf.MacOS.\n\nThe full HiQPdf Next library, which also converts Word, Excel, RTF and Markdown to PDF, comes in the HiQPdf.Next, HiQPdf.Next.Windows, HiQPdf.Next.Windows.Arm64, HiQPdf.Next.Linux, HiQPdf.Next.Linux.Arm64 and HiQPdf.Next.MacOS packages.\n\nMigration guide from Classic to Next:\nhttps://www.hiqpdf.com/hiqpdf-classic-to-next-migration\n\nCompatibility:\n\n* .NET Framework 4.0 and above\n* .NET 10, 9, 8, 7, 6 and .NET Standard 2.0\n* Windows platforms\n* Azure Cloud Services and Azure Virtual Machines\n* Web, Console and Desktop applications\n\nLibrary Features:\n\n* Convert HTML to PDF, images and SVG\n* Convert PDF pages to images and HTML\n* Extract text and images from PDF documents\n* Search text in PDF documents\n* Create PDF documents with text, HTML, SVG, images and graphics\n* Create encrypted, password-protected, digitally signed PDF documents\n* Create PDF documents with forms, text notes, links and JavaScript actions\n* Merge multiple PDF documents into a single one\n* Stamp PDF with HTML, text and images",
